Implementation details:
- `sha256(p)` helper.
- `read(p)`.
- FIND clause: `re.findall(r"(?m)^\s*\(f\)\s+the extension adds points to the future:(.*)$", text)`; assert len==1.
- interior test: `"int(M' minus iota(M))" in clause`.
- Revision history: for each file, find the last `- {index: N, ...}` line and extract; also find all lines containing "clause (f) interior+chronological".
- r3: load JSON, iterate coverage_table rows, find class F2a, look for named_open_findings with id containing "HF-060-EXT-01"; and check "propagating the clause-(f) interior requirement" in required_before_proposal.
- rev14 scope: load map JSON, find assignment event_id == "astra-life08-formulation-rev14", acceptance string; count enumerated items `\((\d)\) `; check if regex `clause\s*\(f\)` present → in_scope.
- Model checker (finite topology): helper interior(U, basis, S), is_connected(U, basis), closure. Models A (boundary-like), B (dense-open), C (genuine interior). Evaluate clause_uninteriored and clause_interiored given M', iotaM, Iplus (a set of pairs), where:
  - clause_uninteriored: ∃q∈iotaM, p∈M'\iotaM with (q,p)∈Iplus
  - clause_interiored: int(M'\iotaM) nonempty AND ∃q∈iotaM, p∈int(M'\iotaM) with (q,p)∈Iplus
- Controls as described.

For model A interior computation: basis = [M, M∪{h1}, M∪{h2}, M'] where M'=M∪H. Note basis elements must be subsets of U. Compute opens = all unions of basis; interior(S) = union of opens O ⊆ S.

